---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const aboutPhoto = '/images/tessa-about-2.jpeg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Tessa Rouse, an MPA candidate, political science graduate, U.S. Army veteran, and emerging public administration and policy professional."
>
  <section class="page-section about-hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1>Public service shaped the path. Policy gave it direction.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          I'm Tessa Rouse, a U.S. Army veteran, political science graduate, and MPA candidate
          at Arizona State University.
        </p>
        <p>
          My work sits at the intersection of policy analysis, public administration,
          organizational systems, data quality, and service delivery. I'm especially interested
          in what happens after a policy is adopted: how institutions interpret it, implement it,
          measure it, and translate it into an experience people can actually navigate.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="about-photo">
        <img src={aboutPhoto} alt="Tessa Rouse smiling in academic regalia" width="256" height="256" />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="container story-grid">
      <div class="section-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">The throughline</p>
        <h2>Systems, responsibility, and implementation.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="story-copy">
        <p>
          I began my professional life in the U.S. Army as a Network Switch Systems Operator.
          The work centered on communications readiness, equipment accountability, operational
          support, and emergency preparedness—including overseas service supporting Patriot
          missile operations.
        </p>
        <p>
          After leaving the Army, I worked in safety, security, emergency response, and
          operational-support environments. Those roles required documentation, adherence to
          policy and procedure, incident coordination, stakeholder communication, and the ability
          to make sound decisions when conditions changed quickly.
        </p>
        <p>
          My later work in emergency response coordination added GIS-based mapping, compliance
          databases, data quality assurance, auditing, reporting, and process improvement. That
          experience helped clarify the kind of work I wanted to pursue long term: understanding
          public systems, finding where they break down, and helping improve how decisions are
          implemented.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section academic-section">
    <div class="container academic-grid">
      <div class="section-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Academic direction</p>
        <h2>From political science to public administration.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="academic-copy">
        <p>
          I earned a B.A. in Political Science, with a concentration in American Government,
          from American Military University in February 2026, graduating Cum Laude.
        </p>
        <p>
          I am now completing a Master of Public Administration at Arizona State University,
          where my graduate work has focused on policy analysis, governance, ethics,
          organizational management, research methods, statistics, implementation, and public
          service.
        </p>
        <p>
          The shift from political science to public administration was deliberate. Political
          science gave me a framework for understanding institutions and power; public
          administration asks the question I find even more compelling: <em>how do we make those
          institutions work well in practice?</em>
        </p>

        <figure class="credential-card">
          <img
            src="/images/amu-diploma.svg"
            alt="American Military University diploma awarded to Tessa Rouse for a Bachelor of Arts in Political Science, Cum Laude, on February 1, 2026"
            width="900"
            height="707"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <figcaption>
            <div>
              <p class="credential-label">Awarded degree</p>
              <strong>B.A. Political Science · Cum Laude</strong>
              <span>American Military University · February 1, 2026</span>
            </div>
            <a
              class="text-link"
              href="https://www.parchment.com/u/s/6mIR"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noreferrer"
            >Verify credential ↗</a>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <!-- preview deployment trigger -->
        <section class="supplemental-credentials" aria-labelledby="supplemental-credentials-title">
          <div class="supplemental-heading">
            <p class="credential-label">Additional credentials</p>
            <h3 id="supplemental-credentials-title">Selected continuing education</h3>
          </div>

          <div class="credential-list">
            <article>
              <div>
                <strong>Using Public Policy for Social Change</strong>
                <span>University of Michigan · Coursera · July 2024</span>
              </div>
              <a class="text-link" href="https://www.coursera.org/account/accomplishments/verify/QT2P58UC5JAN" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Verify ↗</a>
            </article>

            <article>
              <div>
                <strong>Civic Engagement in American Democracy</strong>
                <span>Duke University · Coursera · July 2024</span>
              </div>
              <a class="text-link" href="https://www.coursera.org/account/accomplishments/verify/NRB3YR7VUCB6" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Verify ↗</a>
            </article>

            <article>
              <div>
                <strong>Queering Identities: LGBTQ Sexuality and Gender Identity</strong>
                <span>University of Colorado System · Coursera · July 2024</span>
              </div>
              <a class="text-link" href="https://www.coursera.org/account/accomplishments/verify/ZH8QYWMVJREY" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Verify ↗</a>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section focus-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Current focus</p>
          <h2>The work I want to keep doing.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          I'm building toward policy, program, management, and administrative analysis roles
          where research and evidence can improve public-sector decisions and implementation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="focus-grid">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Policy & program analysis</h3>
          <p>Researching public problems, evaluating alternatives, and translating evidence into useful analysis.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Administrative systems</h3>
          <p>Examining workflows, implementation capacity, organizational responsibility, and administrative burden.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Data & operations</h3>
          <p>Using data quality, GIS support, documentation, and process analysis to strengthen operational decision-making.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="page-section now-section">
    <div class="container now-grid">
      <div class="section-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Now</p>
        <h2>What I'm working on right now.</h2>
        <p class="now-updated">Updated October 2026</p>
      </div>

      <div class="now-card">
        <p class="lede">Master of Public Administration · Arizona State University</p>
        <p class="now-intro">
          Right now, most of my attention is split between graduate study, applied policy
          research, and building toward the kind of public-sector work I want to do long term.
        </p>

        <div class="now-list">
          <article>
            <span>01</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Current coursework</h3>
              <p>
                I've completed my Fall 2026 Session A coursework in
                <strong>Public Service Research I</strong> and <strong>Community Resilience</strong>.
                Session B begins October 14 with <strong>Public Service Research II</strong> and
                <strong>Women, Politics & Public Policy</strong>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span>02</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Academic runway</h3>
              <p>
                I'm enrolled for Spring 2027 in <strong>Public Budgeting and Finance</strong> and
                <strong>Microeconomics of Public Policy I</strong>. My planned summer coursework
                includes <strong>Public Management</strong> and <strong>Community Conflict Resolution</strong>,
                followed by the <strong>Public Affairs Capstone</strong> in Fall 2027.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span>03</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Researching</h3>
              <p>
                I'm especially interested in veterans policy, health policy, administrative
                capacity, organizational change, and the gap between formal policy and the
                experience people have when they encounter public systems.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span>04</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Building toward</h3>
              <p>
                I'm pursuing policy, program, management, and administrative analyst work where
                research, operations, data quality, and public service come together to improve
                implementation and service delivery.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article>
            <span>05</span>
            <div>
              <h3>On the desk</h3>
              <p>
                I'm continuing to develop this portfolio as a living record of my graduate work,
                research, and applied projects—adding pieces when they demonstrate something new
                about how I analyze public problems. I'm also currently awaiting placement as a
                <strong>Graduate Student Assistant at Arizona State University</strong>, an
                potential opportunity to apply my operational, communication, and
                administrative experience in an academic environment. Placement has not yet been confirmed.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <div class="now-links">
          <a class="text-link" href="/writing">Recent writing</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/projects">Current projects</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section personal-section">
    <div class="container personal-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Outside the work</p>
        <h2>Beyond the résumé.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="personal-copy">
        <p class="lede">
          A few of the things that keep me curious when I'm not working or studying.
        </p>
        <p>
          Outside of school and policy work, I'm usually somewhere near a theme park, a
          camera, or a game console. Photography gives me an excuse to pay attention to small
          details; the rest mostly gives my brain somewhere else to go. If I'm on Xbox, you can
          usually find me as <strong>FrauTJ</strong>.
        </p>
        <div class="about-links">
          <a class="text-link" href="/resume">View my résumé</a>
          <a class="text-link" href="/contact">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .about-hero {
    padding-top: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
  }

  .hero-grid,
  .story-grid,
  .academic-grid,
  .personal-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 8rem);
  }

  .hero-grid {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.05fr) minmax(22rem, 0.95fr);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .story-grid,
  .academic-grid,
  .personal-grid {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
  }

  .academic-grid,
  .personal-grid {
    align-items: end;
  }

  .hero-copy > :first-child,
  .academic-copy > :first-child,
  .personal-copy > :first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 821px) {
    .hero-copy h1 {
      font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 5.8vw, 4.35rem);
    }
  }

  .about-photo {
    width: min(100%, 30rem);
    margin: 0;
    justify-self: end;
    position: relative;
  }

  .about-photo::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0.7rem -0.7rem -0.7rem 0.7rem;
    z-index: -1;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    border-radius: 1.35rem;
    background: var(--color-accent-soft);
  }

  .about-photo img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    border-radius: 1.2rem;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
  }

  .hero-copy p:not(.lede),
  .story-copy p,
  .academic-copy > p,
  .personal-copy p:not(.lede) {
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .section-title {
    position: sticky;
    top: 7rem;
    align-self: start;
  }

  .section-title h2,
  .academic-grid h2,
  .personal-grid h2 {
    max-width: 11ch;
  }

  .story-copy {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
  }

  .story-copy p {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .credential-card {
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    border-radius: 1.1rem;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
  }

  .credential-card img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    background: white;
  }

  .credential-card figcaption {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: end;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem 1.1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .credential-card figcaption div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.18rem;
  }

  .credential-label {
    margin: 0 0 0.15rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .credential-card figcaption strong {
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .credential-card figcaption span {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
  }

  .credential-card .text-link {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
  }

  .supplemental-credentials {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
  }

  .supplemental-heading h3 {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
  }

  .credential-list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .credential-list article {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .credential-list article div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.2rem;
  }

  .credential-list strong {
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .credential-list span {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
  }

  .credential-list .text-link {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
  }

  .academic-section,
  .now-section,
  .personal-section {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-bg-deep) 58%, transparent);
  }

  .now-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 8rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .now-grid h2 {
    max-width: 11ch;
  }

  .now-updated {
    margin: 0.85rem 0 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .now-card {
    padding: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 1rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-surface) 94%, transparent);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
  }

  .now-card p:not(.lede) {
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .now-intro {
    margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
  }

  .now-list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .now-list article {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.25rem 1fr;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    padding: 1.15rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .now-list span {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    padding-top: 0.12rem;
  }

  .now-list h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
  }

  .now-list p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
  }

  .now-list strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .now-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem 1.4rem;
    margin-top: 1.2rem;
  }

  .now-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .section-heading {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    align-items: end;
    gap: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .section-heading h2 {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    max-width: 11ch;
  }

  .section-heading > p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .focus-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
  }

  .focus-grid article {
    padding: 1.7rem 1.5rem 0 0;
  }

  .focus-grid article + article {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .focus-grid span {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 2.2rem;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .focus-grid h3 {
    font-size: 1.45rem;
  }

  .focus-grid p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .hero-grid,
    .story-grid,
    .academic-grid,
    .now-grid,
    .personal-grid,
    .section-heading {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      align-items: start;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .about-photo {
      width: min(88vw, 26rem);
      justify-self: start;
      margin-top: 1rem;
    }

    .section-title {
      position: static;
    }

    .credential-card figcaption,
    .credential-list article {
      align-items: start;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .focus-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .focus-grid article,
    .focus-grid article + article {
      padding: 1.5rem 0;
      border-left: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    }

    .focus-grid span {
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
